{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"ab897a9eb6409869082abfea1fa24269b5b5fb81db918b2553d5780b74be09b9","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler inbound link applier","key_entities":["inbound_differ._diff_links_inbound","apply_inbound_records._inbound_update_apply_links","graph/_links.py::add_dependency",".bridge_state/impossible_links.json","rebar.link","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/impossible_links.py","reconcile_helpers._commit_binding_store_snapshot","git_adapter.IMPOSSIBLE_LINKS_FILE"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","inbound links","no convergence","log noise","permanent failures","jira-rebar bridge"],"propositions":["Reconcile Bridge re-attempts structurally-impossible inbound link ADDs (source closed, redundant ancestry, or cycle-creating) identically every pass without recording attempts or failures","The applier catch-and-warn handler has no durable memory, so each pass re-derives and re-attempts the same deterministic verdicts from local graph state","19 doomed rebar.link writes occur per pass (~200+/hour), forming a permanent WARNING floor that obscures real faults","A durable store of impossible links keyed on deciding digests (endpoint and ancestor status/deps) allows skipping re-attempts until structural inputs change","The digest invalidation strategy must be conservative for cycles (global projection keyed, not endpoint-local) to avoid suppressing now-possible links indefinitely"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787457669151254001,"uuid":"085ec32a-7068-40a6-bc11-cd4fac2d5f20"}